# AtaProjectCommon

Full text: `/Users/atakanatabey/Projects/Generator/docs/AtaProjectCommon.md`.

Applies to SharedFrame, StockExchange, Varlik360 and CeyizDefterim. Generator's own source is not produced by this rule. The host is the open project root that contains `.generator/manifest.json`.

- Precedence for file names and locations: if Generator has an output for it (admin skeleton `src/generator-assets/admin-base/_skeleton`, client data layer `docs/frontend/client-data-layer.md`, backend stamps), Generator's name and place win and host code is moved to match. Only where Generator produces nothing does the host rule choose.
- Admin apps never get thunks or slices from Generator (no `client-redux` output in `apps/admin`); every admin is on admin-base + TanStack Query. Thunk / slice generation is for web and mobile only.
- File names are the same in admin, web and mobile: `services/<feature>.service.ts`, `store/thunks/<feature>.thunk.ts`, `store/slices/<feature>.slice.ts` (Generator output adds `.generated` twins). No camelCase variants (`authSlice.ts`, `*.services.ts`, `*Thunks.ts`); older files are renamed when touched. HTTP infrastructure lives in `services/api/` (`index.ts`, `auth.ts`, `hooks.ts`, `platform.ts`; docs/frontend/http-layer.md), so the `services/` root holds only `<feature>.service.ts`.
- Auth is the exception everywhere: Generator cannot generate auth, so auth service / thunk / slice stay hand-written and as they are in every admin, web and mobile app (admin: `auth.slice.ts` with login / me thunks, older admins may keep a separate `auth.thunk.ts`). Do not migrate auth to TanStack or to Generator output.
- Scope: Generator is mandatory for `apps/admin` in every host. In user apps (`apps/web`, `apps/mobile`) it is optional: the data layer (service, thunk, slice) may be generated or hand-written. Files that were generated (`.generated` / first line stamp) are still never edited by hand.
- Do not hand-write generated admin config, stamped backend files, or a new entity admin screen (page, table, service, route) in those hosts. Change the model, then generate.
- Run `node /Users/atakanatabey/Projects/Generator/scripts/host.mjs admin-config <host> [Entity]` or the same command with `generate`. Same functions as the Electron Generate action. `--dry-run` prints paths and writes nothing.
- Admin UI the config cannot express goes in `packages/admin-base` and is checked with `npm run playground` before a host uses it.
- Still hand-written: `*.generated.ts` (`extendResource`), hooks / custom blocks / `*.Custom.cs`, and non-CRUD pages (login, dashboard, logs, metrics, jobs, screen).
